// Title: Potential APT10 Cloud Hopper Activity
// Sigma ID: 966e4016-627f-44f7-8341-f394905c361f
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2017-04-07 | Modified: 2023-03-08
// ATT&CK: execution, G0045, T1059.005
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects potential process and execution activity related to APT10 Cloud Hopper operation
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20180725233601/https://www.pwc.co.uk/cyber-security/pdf/cloud-hopper-annex-b-final.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2017/TA/APT10/proc_creation_win_apt_apt10_cloud_hopper.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".vbs /shell ") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "csvde -f C:\\windows\\web\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".log")
